"text": "The gates: - the lock entries; - the `--locked` workspace build; - escher-driver's unit tests; - the new stand target; - the blitz-tests companions the diff moves; - seven_guis' four process checks; - the capability-statement pin; - the pre-push gate (`fast`); - the `doc` leg. The chunk edits public doc comments (`Defect`, `Reason`, `Session::lint`, the crate doc), and `fast`   runs no rustdoc (test-plan · decision/doc-leg-gates-public-doc-edits); - the `audit` leg. escher-driver takes a dependency, and the fast leg runs no audit; - `stand-repeat`. The new target is a `stand_` file and runs by its glob."
},
{
"from": 280,
"to": 286,
"text": "What is absent: - No boot-path touchpoint changes a binary's start: `session_host.rs` is untouched. `cli_commands`, `mcp_server`,   `host_log` and `mcp_log` drive both binaries' roles and stand in for the smoke. - There is no live leg: no cold-agent run. - There is no headful self-verify harness in this project. - The coverage leg is not run locally. CI's coverage job reads escher-driver's 97 % floor on the pushed tree, and the   CI read below asserts green over it."
},
{
"from": 288,
"to": 288,
"text": "The controls are step 7's one-shot runs, each with its red reading."
},
{
"from": 290,
"to": 291,
"text": "An acceptance reads CI: the windows and macOS test legs hold the planted table's literals and the stand's clean reading. The diff adds no OS-conditional site. The `ci.py` entry's note names what each OS leg witnesses."
}
],
